hat costs ₹65 per kg. What is the ratio in which R1 is mixed with R2?", "options": [{"text": "3 : 4", "added": false}, {"text": "4 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 1", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "alligation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "160", "added": false}, {"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "26", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "7.5 m", "added": false}, {"text": "14 m", "added": false}, {"text": "21 m", "added": false}, {"text": "2.1 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "Which of the following is a prime number?", "options": [{"text": "161", "added": false}, {"text": "171", "added": false}, {"text": "193", "added": false}, {"text": "177", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "types-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "In ΔABC, a line is drawn parallel to BC, intersecting sides AB and AC at Points S and T, where AB = 8.3 cm, BC = 16.6 cm and BS = 5.3 cm. What is the length of ST (in cm)?", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "polynomials-and-factorisation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "The cost price of 10 goods is equal to the selling price of 8 goods. Find the profit percentage.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "S sold his phone for ₹15,500, which he had bought for ₹12,000. What was his percentage profit?", "options": [{"text": "26.67%", "added": false}, {"text": "29.17%", "added": false}, {"text": "32.67%", "added": false}, {"text": "22.67%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A train takes 7 seconds to pass man standing on a platform and another train whose length is double that of the first train, and moving in the opposite direction, takes 10 seconds to pass him. The time taken (in seconds, to the nearest integer) by the trains to pass each other will be:", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "A money lender finds that due to the fall in the annual rate of interest from 18% to 15%, his yearly income diminishes by Rs.750. His capital is:", "options": [{"text": "Rs.25,500", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.25,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.5,000", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.2,500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "Gori and Gopal alone can do a piece of work in 9 and 21 days respectively. In how many days will the work be completed, if they both work on alternate days starting with Gopal?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "Rakhi is 20 years older than her daughter Shikha. In 6 years, Rakhi will be twice as old as Shikha. Therefore, Rakhi’s present age is ____ years.", "options": [{"text": "42", "added": false}, {"text": "37", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A number is increased by 25%, and subsequently decreased by 15%. Find the percentage of net increase or decrease.", "options": [{"text": "7.93% decrease", "added": false}, {"text": "6.25% increase", "added": false}, {"text": "7.23% increase", "added": false}, {"text": "9.18% decrease", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "A football team won 10 games from the total they played. This was 40% of the total. How many games were played in all?", "options": [{"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "The marked price of every item being sold by a wholesaler was ₹400. The wholesaler was offering a stock-clearance sale, under which for every four items paid for, one item was being given free. In addition to that, a further 5% discount on the amount payable on the ‘Buy 4, Get 1 free’ scheme price was being offered to anyone making purchases worth more than ₹15,000. Rameshwar made purchases for which the amount payable, before applying the 5% discount, was ₹16,000. What was the effective discount percentage that was finally offered to Rameshwar during this transaction?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}]}